; The EXT socket, on the far edge beside where the L button and the cart slot are.
;
; +Z points OUT of the shell, which is the convention every port in the room
; follows: the seated plug's shaft goes in along the port's -Z and its shell stays
; outside. Copy this node's transform shape from any other port and a plug still
; seats the right way round. Turned 180 degrees about Y because this face looks
; along -Z.
;
; 1 mm proud of the panel. A seated link plug's origin is the front face of its
; shell, and that face stops almost flush against the socket's rim.
[node name="LinkPort" parent="." instance=ExtResource("9_linkport")]
transform = Transform3D(-1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, -1, -0.045, 0, -0.038)
connector = "agb_link_plug"
